      "content": "There is dignity in accepting what you cannot control, but \"letting go of the struggle\" doesn't have to mean letting go of yourself—it can mean releasing the need to fix everything at once. The peace you're feeling might be a signal that you need a different kind of fight: not against the world, but for your own rest and recovery. You don't have to win every battle today, but you can choose to stay in the game long enough to find a kinder, slower way to play. And that choice, in itself, is a quiet act of strength.",
      "source": "target",
